Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-30
Subject: Guard arm narmcon real-constant narrowing casts
License: expat

`compiler/arm/narmcon.pas` emits ARM real constants into
`current_procinfo.aktlocaldata`, but its overflow/range checks then read back
`current_asmdata.asmlists[al_typedconsts].last` and narrow that base `tai`
node to `tai_real_*bit`.

Under native FPC this old-style cast can slip by unnoticed.  In the translated
C++ stage1 compiler the narrowing cast becomes concrete, and during the
armhf-linux bootstrap `al_typedconsts.last` can still point at an unrelated
`tai_const`.  UBSan then correctly reports the bad downcast while compiling
`rtl/inc/variants.pp`.

Check the node we actually just appended to `aktlocaldata` instead.  That keeps
the range-check logic unchanged while removing the stale-list narrowing cast.

--- a/compiler/arm/narmcon.pas
+++ b/compiler/arm/narmcon.pas
@@ -81,7 +81,7 @@
                   { range checking? }
                   if ((cs_check_range in current_settings.localswitches) or
                     (cs_check_overflow in current_settings.localswitches)) and
-                    (tai_real_32bit(current_asmdata.asmlists[al_typedconsts].last).value=MathInf.Value) then
+                    (tai_real_32bit(current_procinfo.aktlocaldata.last).value=MathInf.Value) then
                     Message(parser_e_range_check_error);
                 end;
 
@@ -95,7 +95,7 @@
                   { range checking? }
                   if ((cs_check_range in current_settings.localswitches) or
                     (cs_check_overflow in current_settings.localswitches)) and
-                    (tai_real_64bit(current_asmdata.asmlists[al_typedconsts].last).value=MathInf.Value) then
+                    (tai_real_64bit(current_procinfo.aktlocaldata.last).value=MathInf.Value) then
                     Message(parser_e_range_check_error);
                end;
 
@@ -106,7 +106,7 @@
                   { range checking? }
                   if ((cs_check_range in current_settings.localswitches) or
                     (cs_check_overflow in current_settings.localswitches)) and
-                    (tai_real_80bit(current_asmdata.asmlists[al_typedconsts].last).value=MathInf.Value) then
+                    (tai_real_80bit(current_procinfo.aktlocaldata.last).value=MathInf.Value) then
                     Message(parser_e_range_check_error);
                 end;
 {$ifdef cpufloat128}
@@ -117,7 +117,7 @@
                   { range checking? }
                   if ((cs_check_range in current_settings.localswitches) or
                     (cs_check_overflow in current_settings.localswitches)) and
-                    (tai_real_128bit(current_asmdata.asmlists[al_typedconsts].last).value=MathInf.Value) then
+                    (tai_real_128bit(current_procinfo.aktlocaldata.last).value=MathInf.Value) then
                     Message(parser_e_range_check_error);
                 end;
 {$endif cpufloat128}
